# Legacy dashboard URLs.
#
# The dashboard used to live at public/dashboard.html, and public/index.html
# was a 455-byte page whose only job was `window.location.replace()`. Reaching
# the dashboard therefore cost three round trips before any content:
#
#   GET /                 -> 455 bytes of HTML the browser had to parse and
#                            execute before it could issue the next request
#   GET /dashboard.html   -> 307 (Cloudflare's own .html -> extensionless
#                            redirect, from the default html_handling)
#   GET /dashboard        -> the actual 33 KB page
#
# The dashboard is now index.html, so '/' serves it directly and new traffic
# pays nothing. These two lines keep old bookmarks working, which is the right
# place for a redirect to cost something.
#
# 301 rather than 302 so browsers cache it and stop asking.
/dashboard       /  301
/dashboard.html  /  301
